# Test: `show plugin conformance run` judges a program from the operator's shell
# VALIDATES: `ze show plugin conformance run "<command>" [name <plugin-name>]`
#   starts the program in declare mode, prints one row per check with its stage
#   and verdict, fails the row that names what the program did wrong with the
#   reason, and exits 0 when no row failed and 1 when one did.
# PREVENTS: a plugin author being told a program conforms when the daemon would
#   refuse it: a failed check rendered as `pass`, a failed report exiting 0 (a
#   script that gates on the status then ships the plugin), or a passing report
#   that no longer says which behaviors nobody judged and so reads as full
#   conformance.
#
# The one question: does what an operator TYPES reach the checker and come back
# as the table and the exit status? The unit tests
# (internal/component/plugin/conformance/conformance_test.go) call Run() with a
# Go struct and read a Go report. They cannot decide whether the run string
# survives as one quoted token, whether `name` reaches the daemon's refusal
# text, whether a failed row is printed at all when the command exits 1, or
# what the process exit status is. Each case below is one class of violation
# from those unit tests, sent through the real command line.
#
# No daemon runs here. The command is a local-data command, so `ze show ...`
# serves it in its own process.
#
# Every expectation sits under the `cmd=` line whose output it describes and
# reads that command's stdout alone (docs/architecture/testing/ci-format.md,
# "Every stream assertion sits under a command and is scoped to it"), and each
# command asserts its own status with `exit=`. A row is asserted with a regex
# that holds the check, its stage and its verdict on ONE line, because a bare
# `contains=pass` is satisfied by any other row.
#
# Each program is a script, because an `exec=` value has no backslash escape:
# a run string that holds both quote characters cannot be written on a `cmd=`
# line. The command starts the program in its own directory, which is the
# test's directory, where the runner writes these files.

# The line the protocol's own writer produces for a plugin with one command
# (validDeclaration, conformance_test.go).
tmpfs=conforming.sh:terminator=EOF_CONFORMING
printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"commands":[{"name":"show query answer","short-help":"Show the answer."}]}'
EOF_CONFORMING

# The same line, and then a status that is not 0.
tmpfs=exits-three.sh:terminator=EOF_EXITS_THREE
printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"commands":[{"name":"show query answer","short-help":"Show the answer."}]}'
exit 3
EOF_EXITS_THREE

# A declaration with no protocol version: the text-era plugin.
tmpfs=no-version.sh:terminator=EOF_NO_VERSION
printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {}'
EOF_NO_VERSION

# printf reads the escapes of its format, so this line ends CR LF.
tmpfs=crlf.sh:terminator=EOF_CRLF
printf '%s\r\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"commands":[{"name":"show query answer","short-help":"Show the answer."}]}'
EOF_CRLF

# A banner on standard output, in front of a declaration that is itself valid.
tmpfs=two-lines.sh:terminator=EOF_TWO_LINES
echo starting up
printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"commands":[{"name":"show query answer","short-help":"Show the answer."}]}'
EOF_TWO_LINES

# A doctor check whose diagnostic code lacks the doctor- prefix
# (validateDoctorCheckDecls, internal/component/plugin/server/startup.go).
tmpfs=doctor-code.sh:terminator=EOF_DOCTOR_CODE
printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"doctor-checks":[{"name":"plugin-ready","phase":"pre-config","codes":["plugin-not-ready"]}]}'
EOF_DOCTOR_CODE

# A command that declares an answer shape ze does not have (the answer-shapes
# case of stage1Cases, internal/component/plugin/server/stage1_checks_test.go).
tmpfs=answer-shape.sh:terminator=EOF_ANSWER_SHAPE
printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"commands":[{"name":"show query answer","shape":"no-such-shape"}]}'
EOF_ANSWER_SHAPE

# --- A conforming program -------------------------------------------------
# Every declare-mode check and every Stage 1 check the declaration reaches
# passes, no row failed, and the command exits 0.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh conforming.sh" name conformance-subject:exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern=program-starts +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=exits-clean +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-decodes +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=doctor-checks +1 +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=answer-shapes +1 +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=help-texts +1 +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=command-names +5 +pass
# A passing report still says what it did not judge, with the reason. Without
# these rows a report with no failure reads as full conformance.
expect=stdout:pattern=tls-connect-back +transport +not-judged +the checker starts no hub
expect=stdout:pattern=schema +schema +not-judged
expect=stdout:pattern=respawn-agreement +1 +not-judged +only a running daemon judges this check
reject=stdout:pattern= (declare|1|5) +fail

# The in-tree mrt plugin, started as its own process the way an operator
# configures it, conforms too: the checker accepts what ze's own SDK writes.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "ze plugin mrt":exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern=program-starts +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-decodes +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=command-names +5 +pass
reject=stdout:pattern= (declare|1|5) +fail

# --- A program that writes nothing -----------------------------------------
# It started and exited 0, so those two rows pass. It declared nothing, so the
# two declaration rows fail, and the Stage 1 rows are not-judged: a row nobody
# could judge is never a pass.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "exit 0" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=program-starts +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=exits-clean +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +fail +the program wrote nothing to standard output
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-decodes +declare +fail +no ze-plugin-engine
expect=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +not-judged +no declaration was read
reject=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +pass

# --- A status that is not 0 -------------------------------------------------
# The declaration is the valid one, so only the exit fails.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh exits-three.sh" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=exits-clean +declare +fail +the program exited 3 in declare mode
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +pass

# --- No protocol version ----------------------------------------------------
# The line is well formed and decodes, so the declare-mode rows pass. The
# refusal is the daemon's own Stage 1 text, and it names the plugin the
# command line named.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh no-version.sh" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-decodes +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +fail +plugin conformance-subject declared no protocol version

# --- A CR LF line ending ----------------------------------------------------
cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh crlf.sh" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +fail +standard output holds a carriage return
expect=stdout:pattern=exits-clean +declare +pass

# --- A second line on standard output ----------------------------------------
# The lenient reader of `show plugin declarations` skips the banner, so the
# declaration still decodes. The strict form is what refuses it.
cmd=foreground:seq=7:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh two-lines.sh" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +fail +standard output holds 2 lines
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-decodes +declare +pass

# --- A declaration a Stage 1 content check refuses ---------------------------
# The line is exactly the strict form, so every declare-mode row passes and
# the failure is the daemon's refusal of what the declaration says.
cmd=foreground:seq=8:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh doctor-code.sh" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=doctor-checks +1 +fail +invalid doctor check: invalid doctor check code
expect=stdout:contains=must start with

cmd=foreground:seq=9:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh answer-shape.sh" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=doctor-checks +1 +pass
expect=stdout:pattern=answer-shapes +1 +fail +invalid answer shape: conformance-subject

# --- A run string that names no program --------------------------------------
# This is a REPORT, not a run that could not happen: the shell started and
# found no such command, so program-starts is the failed row and the command
# exits 1 (queryExitOf, internal/component/plugin/declarations.go; Run,
# conformance.go, "A program that fails to start is a failed row of the
# report, never an error"). Exit 2 is kept for a target the checker refuses
# before it starts anything. Every later row is not-judged, never passed.
cmd=foreground:seq=10:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "/no/such/ze-plugin" name conformance-subject:exit=1
expect=stdout:pattern=program-starts +declare +fail +the run string
expect=stdout:contains=started no program
expect=stdout:pattern=exits-clean +declare +not-judged +the program did not start
expect=stdout:pattern=declaration-line +declare +not-judged
expect=stdout:pattern=protocol-version +1 +not-judged
reject=stdout:pattern= (declare|1|5) +pass
